// The message window fades in and grows over 3 updates (+0x3c bits 14-16 count them, set by FUN_0027e5c0; alpha is 1 - 0.4n,
// scale 1 - 0.1n) and fades out and shrinks over 3 (+0x3d bits 3-5, set by FUN_0027d090; alpha is 0.35n, and the scale is
// multiplied by 0.9 each update). At 60 FPS count 5 and 6 updates with half steps (scale by sqrt(0.9)), and run them on the
// frames the window skips too. The constants for the current speed are copied to 0x81030 from 0x81040 or 0x81050.
patch=1,EE,00081040,word,3EB33333   // 0.35
