// ...and the event script's "wait N frames" command (FUN_001d91f0), which waits N frames and then returns 0, which makes the
// script yield until the next update, so it takes N+1 updates: at 60 FPS wait 2N+1 frames (s0 is the count, s2 counts).
// Scripts that move actors in a loop with "wait 0" (e.g. elevators) would otherwise move them twice as fast.
// Those loops get an actor's position (FUN_001d5990), add to it and set it (FUN_001d5870), so the actor would move every other
// frame: when "wait 0" follows getting and setting the same actor's position in the same script (0x80030 is the actor, 0x80034
// the script, 0x80038 is set if it was set, 0x80039 if it's actor 0, whose position is also stored in the field's +0x150),
// set it halfway between the two positions (0x80000, 0x80010; the halfway one is 0x80020) for the first frame, and to where
// the script set it when the wait ends (0x8003A is set until then, 0x8003C is the actor).
// (0x81DC0-0x81FFF was the boot loader's stack, so caves don't go there. 0x80310-0x80DFF belongs to the 24 arte slots cheat, also
// variables and tables that its build.py writes outside its pnach lines, and 0x80F00-0x80F44 to No damage.)
patch=1,EE,001D94B8,word,08020010   // j 0x80040
patch=1,EE,001D94BC,word,3C020008   // lui v0,0x8
patch=1,EE,00080040,word,904215F8   // lbu v0,0x15F8(v0)
